{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits","id":931408,"title":"Opinions on Mokole Traits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-14T09:34:01-07:00","id":931408,"title":"Opinions on Mokole Traits","content":"Hi everyone,<br /> <br /> I was just wondering what everyone's opinions were for Mokole traits that they get. A lot of them feel lackluster especially when you look at the old list from their small solo book. Horns and Bladed Tail both in particular feel very weak due to their difficulty 7 to hit with no real advantage to them when you can simply claw. And then others feel...strange with how they're worded. Tall comes to mind in that it doubles your height for each point, yet only gives one stamina, which to me feels odd from a story perspective. You can easily be 20 feet tall, and go down almost as easily as any other Fera.<br /> <br /> I understand that I'm looking at them from a strictly mechanical perspective when obviously this is a very story/character driven setting and a lot of these traits add flavor to the characters. But from the purely mechanical aspect, I feel like I'm missing something to make a lot of them truly worthwhile.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:33:50-07:00","id":931516,"title":"","content":"I would argue that horns are actually rather useful when used with a headbutt. this allows you to knock an enemy to the ground (as it works like body slam with a few minor changes) while dealing agg dmg. Tail can be useful if you also took the sacral plexus as well, this gives you two attacks a round that do agg without using Rage (mind you the first purchase is only 4 dice, but still...at a diff 7 the odds of a free attack aren't that bad). <br /> <br /> I'm a big fan of armor (though I think a sufficiently armored mokole should also be rather heavy), and having 1 extra die of dmg for claw and bite attacks are handy. Especially now with how razor claws got altered (Str+5 claw attack at a diff 5). A lot of them however I think are there to add character to your mokole, or are really useful but not in a combat sense (like the aquatic traits). The traits that I didn't like are behemoth, tall and huge size (that was the name right? from the breed book? Mine isn't on me at the moment). Mostly because you can be the size of Godzilla but ...technically the way the system is presented you could have a Garou who's stronger then you. I have read a lot of good suggestions on how to run those traits on this site, but I'm just annoyed that the cannon version didn't actually account for the issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:10:19-07:00","id":931532,"title":"","content":"I can see where you're coming from with Horns since as you said, it does add agg damage to your Headbutt. I think sacral plexus is in the old breed book, yeah? I've only looked at the book briefly and might check with my ST to see what they'll allow from the older book compared to the new Changing Breeds 20 book.<br /> <br /> I do like that a lot of them add flavor, but it's the ones like Fire Breath which does 2 agg (Although can set things on fire if the ST deems something flammable) or as we pointed out the growth ones that while add flavor, don't seem to do much else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:17:06-07:00","id":931536,"title":"","content":"In a Hengeyokai LARP, I played a particularly deadly Zhong Lung with Armor, Long Teeth, Gills, Poison Sacs, and Sacral Plexus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T13:47:54-07:00","id":931554,"title":"","content":"Sacral Plexus is in the breed book. You get 4 dice to make a bonus attack for free with your lower body (such as your tail). For every trait after that you buy, it adds a die. Even then you only have to hit with just 1 success. Average (homid str of 2) Mokole in archid would be dealing 8 dice of agg at zero cost. For most opponents that's really useful (think about it, without gifts or totems stepping in the toughest natural Garou would have an 8 stamina in crinos, and from what I've read Fomor don't tend to be overly armored either, and how often should you be running into vampires with over a 5 Fortitude or Protean 6?).<br /> On another note I'm ok with W20 watering down Mokole venom because they aren't the Anasazi or the Nagah so it doesn't have to be their thing. Not sure how anyone else feels about that. In the breed book a Mokole with that trait and a high investment in it was a brutal killer especially if you add long teeth. <br /> <br /> Also I never liked &quot;Contact Venom&quot;. To be paralyzed in 5 minute intervals per unsoaked successes based on a stamina roll. Think of how long a combat round is, then think of not being able to defend yourself from a raging dragon for 5 minutes worth of rounds. <br /> <br /> Also think about this, these are traits you have with you by just shifting. They may not come off as game breaking, but when you don't have to spend time or resources activating these things, they are handy. Being able to fly or be fully amphibius by just shifting is rather handy. <br /> <br /> (side note: not to be a geek or too technical, just as a big herp hobbiest I have a small pet peeve about the venom/poison confusion so while I know the mokole trait is &quot;poison sacs&quot; I just can't bring myself to call it poison since they describe venom....but &quot;Contact Venom&quot; comes off very much as a poison)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:13:24-07:00","id":931571,"title":"","content":"In a Hengeyokai game I ran back in the early 2000's, one of the players started with 10 gnosis. She decided to spend 8 of those on Huge Size, one point on Contact Poison and one point on Disarticulating Jaw.<br /> <br /> When she would go into her Archid Form, she had 17 Stamina! So anytime she was attacked, she had 17 dice to soak with. This also meant her Contact Poison would be rolling 17 damage to anybody who touched her or that she touched, with each point of damage paralyzing them for 5 minutes. Then she'd just swallow the paralyzed person and eat them.<br /> <br /> She was basically an unstoppable super-tank when she'd go into Archid Form. Of course, this came with the downside was that she was almost 100 feet long, so there were many places where she couldn't assume her Archid form.<br /> <br /> Still, it was a very memorable character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:22:06-07:00","id":931578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931571#post931571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When she would go into her Archid Form, she had 17 Stamina! So anytime she was attacked, she had 17 dice to soak with. This also meant her Contact Poison would be rolling 17 damage to anybody who touched her or that she touched, with each point of damage paralyzing them for 5 minutes. Then she'd just swallow the paralyzed person and eat them.<br /> <br /> She was basically an unstoppable super-tank when she'd go into Archid Form. Of course, this came with the downside was that she was almost 100 feet long, so there were many places where she couldn't assume her Archid form.<br /> <br /> Still, it was a very memorable character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally rest my case on that trait lol <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:24:33-07:00","id":931583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931571#post931571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Hengeyokai game I ran back in the early 2000's, one of the players started with 10 gnosis. She decided to spend 8 of those on Huge Size, one point on Contact Poison and one point on Disarticulating Jaw.<br /> <br /> When she would go into her Archid Form, she had 17 Stamina! So anytime she was attacked, she had 17 dice to soak with. This also meant her Contact Poison would be rolling 17 damage to anybody who touched her or that she touched, with each point of damage paralyzing them for 5 minutes. Then she'd just swallow the paralyzed person and eat them.<br /> <br /> She was basically an unstoppable super-tank when she'd go into Archid Form. Of course, this came with the downside was that she was almost 100 feet long, so there were many places where she couldn't assume her Archid form.<br /> <br /> Still, it was a very memorable character.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why IMO its up to the ST as to whether or not they allow someone to even MAX out their starting Gnosis/will/rage, AND what max # of slots of an archid trait can be taken.. One of my first ST's i played with after the mokole breedbook came out, limited it to 3 slots of huge size max..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:29:31-07:00","id":931589,"title":"","content":"Well in most places where the Mokole stated out (breed book, PGCB and W20 CB) it does say that the archid form is up to GM approval. If the GM approves, have fun, if not...then you'll need another timmy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T15:01:43-07:00","id":931617,"title":"","content":"I think that the Archid form could be up to 170' long, which could cause Delirium to a small city because it would be taller than most of the buildings. It could deal 22+ dice on a Body Slam or Overbear attack. It would also have eight extra health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T15:06:24-07:00","id":931621,"title":"","content":"One thing I could never find...what exactly is an overbear attack? Can anyone tell me that one? I was never sure how to use those dice because I didn't know what it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T17:31:25-07:00","id":931713,"title":"","content":"SO thinking on some of the less...inspiring traits (*cough* duckbill *cough*) I remember one time pointing out a few I didn't see as that great, and my GM at the time said that it was for NPC Mokole...so every Mokole isn't a combat monster, and the PC's could have clutch mates to protect. Anyone's thoughts on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T18:24:56-07:00","id":931737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931713#post931713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SO thinking on some of the less...inspiring traits (*cough* duckbill *cough*) I remember one time pointing out a few I didn't see as that great, and my GM at the time said that it was for NPC Mokole...so every Mokole isn't a combat monster, and the PC's could have clutch mates to protect. Anyone's thoughts on that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree with your ST that they were for NPC Mokole, on the grounds that I just don't see them doing what the mechanical note claims that they do. They're in &quot;Tall adds dice to Perception&quot; territory. Especially for a duck bill, since it seems like something cosmetic; even if it aids in shoveling up soil, there might not be a mechanical benefit to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T20:28:54-07:00","id":931782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931737#post931737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would disagree with your ST that they were for NPC Mokole, on the grounds that I just don't see them doing what the mechanical note claims that they do. They're in &quot;Tall adds dice to Perception&quot; territory. Especially for a duck bill, since it seems like something cosmetic; even if it aids in shoveling up soil, there might not be a mechanical benefit to it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, so do you think they were just traits that weren't really well thought out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:38:49-07:00","id":931806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931782#post931782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, so do you think they were just traits that weren't really well thought out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. Most of them probably weren't very well-vetted, as one can tell through the Huge Size/Contact Poison exploit, but unlike duck bills and back sails, those other traits did something highly advantageous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:20:17-07:00","id":931822,"title":"","content":"So, besides me, anyone made up their own mokole archid form traits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T22:21:17-07:00","id":931823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931782#post931782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, so do you think they were just traits that weren't really well thought out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It seems pretty clear that the author wrote those traits more with flavor in mind than mechanical usefulness. I would point towards traits like Crop, or Store Food or Snorkel. Those might be interesting and flavorful, but I can't imagine a player seriously wanting to take those.<br /> <br /> About half the traits are fairly useful in most games, the other half or so are fairly worthless in most games, and a tiny minority are either way too strong or worthless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-15-2016, 01:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T09:54:04-07:00","id":932547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=931621#post931621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I could never find...what exactly is an overbear attack? Can anyone tell me that one? I was never sure how to use those dice because I didn't know what it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that Overbear is the equivalent of Body Slam, except that it is against a smaller opponent. Think of it as a trample attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T10:38:28-07:00","id":932557,"title":"","content":"Alright that makes sense...It used to drive me up a wall. I had one GM rule you got bonus dice to dmg anytime you were bigger then your opponent but I wasn't sure if that was right either due to &quot;Overbear&quot; never being actually described in cannon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:19:47-07:00","id":932591,"title":"","content":"That makes it pretty OP, doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:23:30-07:00","id":932592,"title":"","content":"But is it anymore OP then being paralyzed for minutes at a time in combat? Although I do agree with you, it seemed to much to be true...because take huge size only once and you're larger then damned near everything in the WoD. Its why I never got behind Huge Size (because of how my old GM played it then me realizing the whole strength issue I brought up earlier), or Contact Venom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T17:24:46-07:00","id":932688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/931408-opinions-on-mokole-traits?p=932547#post932547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that Overbear is the equivalent of Body Slam, except that it is against a smaller opponent. Think of it as a trample attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>The maneuvers are rather mixed up. Body slam actually describes hoisting someone up and slamming them. I can't recall if there was another maneuver that fit better, but there's some vague inkling I have that M20 actually had cleaner terminology for things like head butts and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T17:34:17-07:00","id":932694,"title":"","content":"Probably. In any case, I would rule that it was a slamming attack to knock down a target.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T17:36:30-07:00","id":932695,"title":"","content":"Its odd Mage would have the cleaner system...or it feels odd at least...this is why I'd like an updated combat book. I'm not a fan of the old one and we have odd things like &quot;overbear&quot; hanging around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T08:07:26-07:00","id":956970,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on my Mokole? <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nw-SpC8DyR6GwNa6b7p1mnY5pft3aaEe0zRZ8RckzVI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nw-SpC8DyR6GwNa6b7p1mnY5pft3aaEe0zRZ8RckzVI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nw-SpC8DyR6GwNa6b7p1mnY5pft3aaEe0zRZ8RckzVI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Nw-SpC8DyR6GwNa6b7p1mnY5pft3aaEe0zRZ8RckzVI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Currently running her in a Rage Across Australia game, didn't really build her to be the mechanical beast she could be, was more interested in making her interesting.<br /> <br /> Also recommended gifts and such would be nice! Or anything I missed/math'd incorrectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:00:49-07:00","id":957136,"title":"","content":"Looks nice.... Loved the taking of the flaws to round out the beast side of her merits..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T13:16:51-07:00","id":957150,"title":"","content":"Only snag is that to be able to stand in Archid you technically need the upright walking archid trait. I only mention it because you mention that she can stand to fight...I never liked that you had to pay to stand up right like all the shifters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T21:17:51-07:00","id":957391,"title":"","content":"I viewed it as being unable to move while upright but being in place allows minor standing like bears or some dinosaurs. Also being quadruped is better for tackling since if I fail dex + ath to keep my feet I still get up automatically next turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:11:45-07:00","id":957505,"title":"","content":"Alright, I can see that. I grew up on the breed book which states it's to free up the for limbs for tool use, while the CB20 says it allows for freed limbs when walking. So really it's a GM call, especially when you take into account how in the old breed book archid traits were from remembering different creatures and upright walking references monitors, who rear up to look around or will do it when fighting each other (similar to how you described things), and not to walk around.<br /> <br /> I do have an idea though...I wouldn't worry too much about tackling, but instead use the headbutt manuver, and I'd totally go whole on hog the archid depiction of a Kaprosuchus (see what I did there?) And buy both long teeth and horns. Then ask my gm to interpret this as having tusks. Thus way you can head butt, knock enemies over and do agg all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 08-25-2016, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T17:35:05-07:00","id":988531,"title":"","content":"Do folks know of perhaps some fan made or balanced versions of Archid Traits? I love the idea of being able to have a form that's dreamt up. But I always felt the ways you did or was interested in seeing a lot more variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}